        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The offseason for the Toronto Maple Leafs isn't a quiet pause - it's a storm of reshuffling, with <strong>Daniel Alfredsson joining the rival Maple Leafs</strong> as the headline that redefines the team's identity. After finishing 78 points and 8th in the Atlantic, the Leafs are now in full draft and free agency mode, chasing depth and cap flexibility. The signing of young RFA William Vnuv to a two-year, $875,000 two-way deal signals a commitment to building from within, while the front office weighs bold trades and veteran additions. With Dylan Larkin's trade request still simmering, the roster's future hinges on who stays and who walks. <strong>The next move - whether it's a trade, a free-agent splash, or a draft-night gamble - will shape the Leafs' path back to the Atlantic's top tier.</strong>",
