      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Something electric has ignited in the Blue Jays' bullpen and bats, turning a sluggish stretch into a <strong>dominant 10-0 shutout of the Giants</strong> on July 8, capped by Dylan Cease's no-hitter bid into the ninth. Now riding a two-game win streak, the team sits at 44-49, third in the AL East, yet just 11.5 games behind the division lead - a gap that feels suddenly bridgeable. Cease, the story of the night, earned rare praise from the Jays after losing his no-hit bid on a ninth-inning walk, while Kazuma Okamoto's first-career grand slam in the opener broke the game open early. The lineup is clicking, the pitching is ferocious, and the momentum is real. <strong>Next up: a Friday night showdown at the Padres, where the Jays must prove this surge isn't just a fluke against a weak opponent.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 9, 2026"
      },
